# Rocdown

Rocdown is Markdown with an optional `@page` header. Write documentation
that way, then add a `rocdown.toml` when you want a site. Live pages that
reuse Applications are an experimental extra.

Until an installed `rocdown` exists, prefix each `rocdown` command with
`cargo run -q -p rocci-rocdown-cli --` from the repository root.

````rocdown
@page {
    meta: {
        title: "Hello",
        description: "A small Markdown page",
    },
}

# Hello

This paragraph is ordinary Markdown.

:note[title: "Optional"] {{
    Asides, figures, and tabs are article blocks. They stay Markdown-first.
}}
````

Static pages stay Markdown. Hydrate and live pages come later.

You do not need Rocdown to ship an application. This layer is
**experimental** — more so than templates.

:figure[caption: "A static Rocdown site is catalogued in Rust and wrapped in one compiled theme."] {{
